{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כפה", :translit "kafah", :gloss "her hand"} {:he "דין", :translit "din", :gloss "judgment"} {:he "כפה פרשה לעני", :translit "kafah parashah la'ani", :gloss "her hand, the section about the poor"} {:he "מה להלן ממון אף כאן ממון", :translit "mah lehalan mamon af kan mamon", :gloss "just as there money, so here too money"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כפה" "כפה"]}], :frame {:text "The word כפה appears two times in Scripture. One occurrence is here in Deuteronomy 25:12 in the context of judgment (דין). The phrase 'כפה פרשה לעני' refers to the other occurrence, in Deuteronomy 15:7–8, where the context is the command to open your hand to the poor. Just as the occurrence about the poor concerns money, so the occurrence here also concerns money, implying the penalty is monetary compensation rather than literal severing.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 25:12" "Deuteronomy 15:7–8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עינך", :translit "eynekha", :gloss "your eye"} {:he "לא יהיה לך בכיסך", :translit "lo yihyeh lekha bikisekha", :gloss "you shall not have in your pouch"} {:he "עינך לא יהיה לך בכיסך", :translit "eynekha lo yihyeh lekha bikisekha", :gloss "your eye shall not be in your pouch"} {:he "כי אין הברכה מצויה אלא בדבר הסמוי מן העין", :translit "ki ein ha-berakhah metsuyah ela ba-davar ha-samui min ha-ayin", :gloss "for blessing is found only in a thing hidden from the eye"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah-style linkage via verbal analogy between עינך and the adjacent phrase לא יהיה לך בכיסך, interpreting proximity as hermeneutic connection."}], :frame {:text "The principle that blessing is found only in something hidden from the eye derives from the Talmudic discussion: after the evil eye was given dominion over things that are counted, blessing rests only on what is concealed. The Sages infer this from the verse 'The eye did not see, God besides You' (Isaiah 64:3) and from the account of the manna in the wilderness, where blessing was present because the quantity was unknown and uncounted.", :sources ["Bava Metzia 42a" "Ta'anit 8b" "Isaiah 64:3" "Exodus 16:4–18"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וקצותה את כפה", :translit "u-ketzotah et kafah", :gloss "and you shall cut off her hand"} {:he "לא יהיה לך בכיסך", :translit "lo yihyeh lekha bikisekha", :gloss "you shall not have in your pouch"} {:he "דבר המוטל בכיס", :translit "davar ha-mutal ba-kis", :gloss "a matter placed in the pouch"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semantic inference: proximity to בכיסך ('in your pouch') teaches that the phrase וקצותה את כפה refers to money, since money is what resides in a pouch."}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Ishmael interprets 'and you shall cut off her hand' (Deuteronomy 25:12) as a monetary penalty rather than literal amputation, understanding the verse to mean payment evaluated by the court. The word יד ('hand') elsewhere carries the meaning of payment, as in 'I have made your wages מתנה ('a gift') in my hand' (Genesis 33:10), supporting the reading that the penalty is financial compensation.", :sources ["Mekhilta d'Rabbi Yishmael Mishpatim 8" "Bava Kamma 28b" "Genesis 33:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כפה" "כפה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כפה", :refs ["Deuteronomy 25:12" "Isaiah 9:13" "Isaiah 19:15" "Proverbs 31:20"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כפה", :refs ["Deuteronomy 25:12" "Isaiah 9:13" "Isaiah 19:15" "Proverbs 31:20"], :n 4, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah-style linkage via verbal analogy between עינך and the adjacent phrase לא יהיה לך בכיסך, interpreting proximity as hermeneutic connection.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semantic inference: proximity to בכיסך ('in your pouch') teaches that the phrase וקצותה את כפה refers to money, since money is what resides in a pouch.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:29.002441984Z", :model "glm-5.2"}